From: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:13:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] [3.1.1] [M156] [PDF] Reject re-entrancy in
 PDFiumPage::Unload()

Original change's description:
> [PDF] Reject re-entrancy in PDFiumPage::Unload()
>
> Trying to unload in the middle of an unload is a bonehead maneuver. Add
> a new `is_unloading_` bit to check for this and make re-entrant calls
> into no-ops.
>
> Also set `available_` to false for the same duration for good measure.
> Check `is_unloading_` in MarkAvailable() to avoid unexpected changes to
> this member variable.
>
> Also mark `engine_` as const along the way.
>
> Fixed: 583268206
> Change-Id: Ia4c9c7ddb4c28261a71437c6a86cf119dd15f007
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8778185
> Reviewed-by: Tom Sepez <tsepez@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1740744}

